# This governs the build CONTEXT, not COPY. Everything under backend/ is
# packaged and sent to the Docker daemon before the first instruction runs, so
# excluding a file here is stronger than merely declining to COPY it: an excluded
# file never leaves the machine, and cannot end up in an image layer by accident.

# 75 MB of build output, and the jar the image builds for itself anyway.
target/

# Secrets. .env is gitignored, which says nothing about Docker - without this
# line a local .env would be shipped into the context and readable by any
# instruction in the build.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Evidence and reports, including Dependency-Check output.
reports/
*.log
dependency-check-suppressions.xml

# Editor and OS noise.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Kept in the context deliberately: pom.xml, src/, mvnw and .mvn — the build
# stage needs all four, and dropping any of them breaks the first COPY rather
# than merely slowing the build down.
